{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "HVA Depth Guard",
  "description": "Before any write operation to Python files, verify the content doesn't introduce HEA ansatz or HVA depth p>2. These are non-negotiable architectural constraints (Mele et al. 2026).",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "preToolUse",
    "toolTypes": [
      "write"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "Before completing this write, check the content for violations of the two non-negotiable circuit constraints: (1) HVA only — never HEA. Flag any usage of EfficientSU2, RealAmplitudes, TwoLocal, or any reference to 'HEA' as ansatz. (2) Circuit depth p must be ≤ 2 layers. Flag any p_layers > 2, p > 2, or n_layers > 2 in HVA/circuit context (not MPNN layers which can be higher). If the file being written is not quantum-circuit-related (e.g., documentation, config, MPNN-only code), respond '✅ No circuit constraints apply'. If violations found, explain why they violate the Mele et al. depth truncation principle and suggest the correct approach."
  }
}
